The ONLY paragraph connection decision. Set true when this text literally completes the preceding paragraph, including a sentence from the previous page. A figure and its captions before this text do not make it a new body paragraph: on the FIRST main TEXT after such labels, join=true still appends to the preceding-page body cursor. A literal unfinished clause and its completion are ONE paragraph, not a new paragraph merely because a page/image intervened. A genuinely new printed paragraph is false. Decide within this destination, not against physical neighbours or captions. Assets themselves are false. No outgoing flag is submitted.
